### The final implementation order is also included

```text
CP-HS0   repair Dell
CP-HS1   TaskSpec throughout factory
CP-HS2   LiteLLM gateway
CP-HS3   Dell candidate-route API
CP-HS4   deterministic HotSwap
CP-HS5   quota ledger
CP-HS6   Hermes adapter
CP-HS7   failure classifier
CP-HS8   outcome learner
CP-HS9   account opportunity queue
CP-HS10  shadow benchmark
CP-HS11  low-risk free-first rollout
CP-HS12  coding rollout
CP-HS13  bandit
CP-HS14  verified cascade
CP-HS15  contextual router
CP-HS16  runtime measurements → Dell
CP-HS17  production certification
```

The key end-state is:

> **VentureLab stops choosing models. It describes the job. Dell knows the market. HotSwap decides the economically optimal route. LiteLLM supplies the credentials and provider abstraction. Hermes executes and survives failover. VentureLab grades the result. Those outcomes make the next routing decision better.**

That closes the loop.

